{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And now write, etc.</b> The verse's saying ״וְעַתָּה״ (and now): even though Moses would not have delayed to fulfill the word of HaShem immediately and at once, the intention was to spur him to write immediately and at once, before commanding Joshua as stated in the adjoining verse, where it is written (Deuteronomy 31:14): ״קְרָא אֶת יְהוֹשֻׁעַ״ — for even though the occasion was meant for commanding Joshua, where it is written ״קְרָא אֶת יְהוֹשֻׁעַ וְגוֹ׳ וַאֲצַוֶּנּוּ״, nevertheless HaShem desired to give precedence to the writing of the song and teaching it." "<b>And likewise</b> you will find that the verse states (Deuteronomy 31:22): ״וַיִּכְתֹּב מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַשִּׁירָה וְגוֹ׳ וַיְלַמְּדָהּ״ etc., and afterward it says: ״וַיְצַו אֶת יְהוֹשֻׁעַ״ etc. — which means that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Joshua and strengthened him to bring Israel. And it would have been proper for Him to complete every utterance, blessed be He, that He commanded, and only afterward for them to fulfill His commandments to write the song and teach it. Rather, the reason is that HaShem commanded to write and to teach immediately, and this urgency came only so as not to delay until He would command Joshua." "<b>and teach it, etc. Put it in their mouth, etc.</b> Three commandments did HaShem command: first, to write. Second, to teach it to the children of Israel so that they would know the intent of the words of the song. Third, to put it in their mouth, to know its reading." "<b>And all three</b> Moses performed, as it is written: ״וַיִּכְתֹּב מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַשִּׁירָה״ (Deuteronomy 31:22). Second: ״וַיְלַמְּדָהּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״. Third: ״וַיְדַבֵּר מֹשֶׁה בְּאָזְנֵי כָל קְהַל יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת דִּבְרֵי הַשִּׁירָה הַזֹּאת״ (Deuteronomy 31:30) — meaning, he read it aloud to them by way of chanting, so that they would know to recite it in the manner that he recited it to them, and this is what the verse means by ״שִׂימָהּ בְּפִיהֶם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:00.660735885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}